Okay, it's not really a new idea; in fact, I found an old thread on
the subject via Google Groups:

http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&lr=&ie=UTF-8&oe=UTF-8&safe=images&th=2aeab2e760ba74bd&rnum=7

I've been working on my own implementation of this class for NetHack,
and even have a preliminary version of it working (still needs a lot
of work including the quest).

Anyway, I wanted to tap this newsgroup for ideas on some aspects of
the class:

 - Mythology: I had a hard time deciding this, but went for Irish
Celtic, with Ogma as lawful, Dagda as neutral, and Aine as chaotic. 
In fact, I was thinking of having Jesters share the same "universe" as
knights, just because they both serve kings, etc.

Anyone have any alternate suggestions?

 - The Quest: Not sure on this one, but if I go with Irish Celtic
mythology, then maybe I can do something out of Irish folklore for the
quest, perhaps.  Maybe something involving the Unseelie Court?  It
would have to be some kind of Fool's Errand, for certain.  ;-)

 - Quest Item: Not certain on this one, either, but maybe a book
containing the world's funniest joke?  Carried: gives free action,
invoked: causes non-mindless monsters in area to laugh for several
turns (confusion or stun, in nethack terms), read: boosts spell
energy.

Any other good ideas for the quest or quest item?

 - Alignment: N,C
 - Races: Human, Gnome

These make sense to people?  I can't pitcure a lawful jester or even
an elf jester, personally.

 - Weapon skills: knife(E), club(E), boomerang(E), *mace(E),
dagger(S), dart(s), **whip(s), short sword(b), quarterstaff(b),
sling(b), bow(b)
 - Spell skills: enchantment(E), escape(E), divination(b)

*-Expert in mace because jesters start with a bauble - a jester's
scepter - , which I put in the mace class of weapons.

**-Skilled in whip becase rubber hoses are in the whip class

I figured that jesters would be good with normal juggling implements,
as well as silly weapons.  For spells, I think they'd be best at
mind-affecting spells as well as ones that get them out of trouble.

 - Level titles: Buffoon, Wit, Comic, Joker, Clown, Laughingstock,
Jackass, Trickster, Fool

Do these sound good to people?

 - Luck: I was thinking that a luck bonus might be appropriate, but
I'm not sure.  Perhaps only when the jester is wearing his jester's
outfit and, or wielding his bauble?  This way, it would likely just be
an early game benefit, since these would likely get discarded for
better items later-on.

Any alternate suggestions on this?

Finally, is there any interest in such a class?  Even if there's not,
I'll likely finish making it for my own amusement, but there would be
no need to announce it if there's no interest.  :-)


